  "notes": [
   "This page shows steps 1-8 at tiny scale; only steps 1-2 were clear enough to record with confidence.",
   "Step 1: dark bluish gray side-finger hinge plate (b1) sits under the left edge of the black 4x4 plate (b2).",
   "Step 2: four red 2-finger hinge plates (b3-b6) are attached to the underside of b2 around its edges (viewed from below). Exact studs not determinable, so ports are null.",
   "Steps 3-8 (more legs, light gray and orange plates, levers as antennae, red wedge plates, black 2x2/2x3/2x4 plates, orange tail sub-assembly) were too small to identify reliably and are not recorded.",
   "Page 2 is a promotional page showing the crab combined with other sets. It has no building steps, so nothing was added.",
   "These are additions only; b1-b6 from the earlier answer stay as they were.",
   "Piece counts now match the parts list: 2540 x1, 298c02 x2, 3020 x2, 3021 x1, 3022 x2, 3023 x6 orange/red, 3623 x1, 41769 x1, 41770 x1, 44301a x6, 44302a x7 (6 red, 1 dark bluish gray), 44567a x1, 3031 x1.",
   "The first page's drawings are tiny, so placements for steps 3-8 are best estimates. Which piece sits on which, and the exact studs, are guesses, so most ports are null.",
   "The six red 44302a pieces (b3-b8) are the leg bases. Each takes one black 44301a leg tip by hinge.",
   "b28 (second black 2x4) is placed beside b15 in step 3 to cover the 4x4 base. This is an assumption.",
   "The tail sub-assembly in the step 8 inset is built as b29 (dark gray hinge), b30 (red 1x2), b27 (black 2x3) and orange 1x2 plates. It hinges to b1 at the rear.",
   "The orange 1x2 plates are b17, b18, b22, b31 and b32. b31 and b32 are the plates on top of the tail."
  ]
 },
